  "body": "# Setups page: two orientation dropdowns (plane + point), same section everywhere\n\n## What\n\nThe setup alignment UI is scattered across five separate sections\n(preset/angles picker, lay-on-plane row, lay-on-points row, part-axes\nrows, work-offset label). Collapse it into ONE section with TWO\ndropdowns, drawn identically wherever a setup's orientation is edited:\n\n- **Plane orientation** - how the part's frame is set:\n  `Axes` (the two-pick 3D alignment, #769), `Points` (the three-point\n  lay, #555), `Face` (the face lay, #330), `Cylinder angle` (NEW: two\n  curved-face picks give a bore/cylinder axis; it lands on a chosen\n  world axis, turned by an angle about it), `Manual` (the preset combo\n  and typed angles, #326/#606).\n- **Orientation point** - where the setup's WCS origin sits:\n  `From model box` (the parts' bounds - corner or centre), `From stock\n  box` (the setup's stock bounds - corner or centre), `Manual point`\n  (pick a vertex in the viewport). Placing the point keeps the WCS's\n  rotation: the frame comes from the plane dropdown, the point only\n  moves the origin.\n\nSelecting an entry expands its controls below the dropdown. Existing\nfunctions are reused verbatim as the expanded content; the completing\nwork is the cylinder-angle backend and the per-setup origin placement.\n\n## Everywhere the same\n\nThe section is one component mounted in BOTH places that edit a\nsetup's orientation: the Setups overview (every setup stacked) and each\nsetup's own Settings page. Same dropdowns, same options, same look.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Both pages show the same two dropdowns; picking an option expands\n  exactly that option's controls; the old flows still work through\n  them (the row functions keep their own entry points, so their\n  existing tests stay green untouched).\n- `Cylinder angle`: two curved-face picks on a bore land its axis on\n  the chosen world axis with the typed angle about it; refusals by\n  name (same face twice, coincident centroids, non-finite).\n- The orientation point places the named setup's WCS origin (corner /\n  centre of the model or stock box, or a picked vertex), rotation kept;\n  undo restores. Inactive setups place their own WCS, not the active\n  one's.\n- UI tests: the section expands, both mount points draw it, the origin\n  lands per setup.\n",
